-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",19,{
[577]="700544B9\n1\tFind a bit of resilient mould (total: 3)\030Find a speck of glimmering salt (total: 3)\030Find some Agarnaith fruit (total: 3)\tResilient mould, glimmering salt, and Agarnaith fruit can all be found in Minas Morgul. You should recover these ingredients.\n2\tGrind up the ingredients with a mortar and pestle at Barad Orhant\tA mortar and pestle can be found at Barad Orhant. You should grind up the ingredients.\n3\tRemove the potential remedy from the mortar and pestle\tA mortar and pestle can be found at Barad Orhant. You should remove the potential remedy from the mortar and pestle.\n4\tSick Rangers can be found in Barad Orhant. You should treat the Rangers with the potential remedy.\t\n5\tTalk to Arodor in Barad Orhant\tArodor can be found in Barad Orhant. You should talk to Arodor.\n",
[578]="7005A99F\n1\tAppraise the banded gold\030Appraise the copper\030Appraise the amethyst\030Appraise the marble\tVarious stones can be found nearby in Asbaj-khîrfin. You should appraise each of the various stones.\n2\tTalk to Dargumë\tDargumë can be found in Asbaj-khîrfin. You should talk to Dargumë.\n3\tCollect banded gold (total: 12)\tBanded gold can be found in northern Máttugard. You should collect banded gold.\n4\tBring the banded gold to Dargumë\tDargumë can be found at Asbaj-khîrfin. You should bring the banded gold to Dargumë.\n",
[579]="7002EF49\n1\tDefeat Mokrûk\t\n2\tDefeat Mokrûk\tMokrûk, captain of the Enemy's mounted scouts, may be found somewhere in the northern part of the Entwash Vale. You should find and defeat Mokrûk, captain of the Enemy's mounted scouts.\n3\tTalk to Béortnoth outside of Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped beyond the walls of Thornhope. You should return to Thane Béortnoth with news of Mokrûk's defeat.\n",
[580]="70032BF4\n1\tDefeat Durub Orcs at Gazatu-ru (total: 10)\tDurub Orcs can be found at Gazatu-ru, south of the Twenty-first Hall. Dómárr has asked you to show the Durub that they are not welcome in the Great Hall of Durin.\n2\tTalk to Dómárr\tDómárr is resting at a small camp-fire in the Great Hall of Durin, south of the Twenty-first Hall. Dómárr will be pleased to hear that the ranks of the Durub have been thinned.\n",
[581]="70059325\n1\tTalk to Nellie Boskins\tNellie Boskins is in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Nellie Boskins about the altercation.\n2\tFind the scene of the altercation\tThe place of the altercation can be found in Trestlebridge. You should find the scene of the altercation.\n3\tUse Blood\tThe place of the altercation can be found in Trestlebridge. You should investigate the scene of the altercation.\n4\tFollow the faint trail of blood\tThe start of the faint trail of blood can be found in Trestlebridge. You should follow the trail and find out where it leads.\n5\tThe small shed can be found by the river, near Trestlebridge. You should investigate the scene around the small shed.\t\n6\tThe small shed can be found by the river, near Trestlebridge. You should search nearby for more evidence.\t\n7\tSearch the Wildwood for the murder suspect\tWhoever murdered the guard must have gone down-stream on a small boat. You should search down-stream in the Wildwood for the murder suspect.\n8\tConfront the murder suspect\tThe potential murder suspect can be found in the northern part of the Wildwood. You should confront the murder suspect.\n9\tLock up the murderer in the pillory at Trestlebridge\tYou should return to Trestlebridge and lock up the brigand in the pillory.\n10\tTalk to the weary brigand in Trestlebridge\tThe weary brigand can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to the weary brigand.\n11\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n12\tSurvey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge\tReconstruction work continues in Trestlebridge. You should survey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge.\n13\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n",
[582]="7003085A\n1\tApproach the old crofter\t\n2\tApproach the old crofter\tThe old crofter is just ahead, standing atop a cliff to the south of Snowbourn.\n3\tDefeat the Orc attackers (total: 2)\tThe Orc attackers have moved to attack the elderly crofter standing atop a cliff to the south of Snowbourn.\n4\tTalk to the old crofter\tThe crofter is standing alone on a cliff overlooking a waterfall to the south of Snowbourn.\n",
[583]="7002EF7A\n1\tDefeat Zân\tZân can be found at the goblin-camp of Thrug-unur, north-east of Éomer's Vengeance. The mysterious old man suggested that you defeat Zân, the captain of the Moria-goblins, in hopes of cutting off the reinforcements from Thornhope.\n2\tTalk to the mysterious old man at Éomer's Vengeance\tThe mysterious old man can be found at Éomer's Vengeance, south-west of Thrug-ulur. You should return to the mysterious old man with news of your success.\n",
[584]="7004A904\n1\tMine glowing ore (total: 10)\tGlowing ore can be found inside Kâm Lagúrz, the Brokencleft. You should mine the glowing ore for Atli Spider-bane.\n",
[585]="7002C4BD\n1\tFind Idmar and his men\tIdmar and his scouts are along the road to the south-east. Brifard requests that you head south-east to meet his captain, Idmar, who has travelled with his men to deal with a mysterious task.\n2\tExamine the fallen soldier\tYou have come across a fallen Rohirrim. You should examine him and determine what fate befell him.\n3\tSearch the road for Idmar and his men\tUncertain what remains of the scouting party Brifard mentioned, you should continue south-east along the road and search for Idmar or any other Rohirrim.\n",
[586]="70016B2E\n1\tFind and speak to Jari\tJari is just west of the entrance of Tunzelgund, east of the Shadowed Refuge. Klintur has asked you to accompany Jari in his search for answers regarding the madness of the spiders.\n2\tTalk to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge\tKlintur is at the Shadowed Refuge. You should return to Klintur and tell him of the terrifying creature you encountered with Jari.\n",
[587]="70067F74\n1\tSearch for the creature that defends the woods of Jâghimsa\030Return the phials of huorn sap to Tankho\030Collect phials of sap from moving trees ([see journal]/10)\tMake your way north and east through the woods in the shadow of the mountains outside of Rakhatâb and search for evidence of the creature the workers say dwells at Jâghimsa. Collect the sap from the moving trees within the wood.\n",
[588]="70069070\n1\tDefeat Umbari Wildwoods (total: 6)\030Defeat Umbari Huorns (total: 8)\tYou've been asked to trim back the onslaught of huorns pillaging along the roads of the Cape of Umbar.\n2\tFind and fell the Great Huorn\tFell the Great Huorn.\n3\tFind the Scout\t\n",
[589]="7003E461\n1\tCollect slime from Entwash-slugs (total: 8)\tSlugs can be found in western Fangorn along the shores of the river Entwash. Quickbeam's Huorn wants you to heal wounded trees in Fangorn with slug-slime.\n2\tWounded trees can be found in western Fangorn along the shores of the river Entwash.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have healed many trees with slug-slime.\n",
[590]="7005242E\n1\tGather yellow cattails around the festival grounds (total: 8)\tYellow cattails can be found around the edges of the Bree-land Festival Grounds. Nethlas asked a hobbit to gather up yellow cattails for him to study, and the hobbit never returned. Now he has asked you to complete the task.\n2\tBring the yellow cattails to Nethlas at the festival grounds\tNethlas, new apprentice of the herb-master at Minas Tirith, is waiting for you to bring him yellow cattails at the Bree-land Festival Grounds.\n3\tPick up the spring wine at the festival grounds\tNethlas requested a delivery of spring wine for his table of herbalists. The wine bottles should be on the other side of the festival grounds.\n4\tTalk to Nethlas at the festival grounds\tNethlas is by the herbalists' table at the festival grounds.\n5\tGather purple Anorloth around the festival grounds (total: 8)\tPurple Anorloth can be found around the edges of the Bree-land Festival Grounds.\n6\tBring the purple Anorloth blooms to Nethlas at the festival grounds\tNethlas, new apprentice of the herb-master at Minas Tirith, is waiting for you to bring him purple Anorloth blooms at the Bree-land Festival Grounds.\n7\tPick up the spring wine at the festival grounds\tNethlas requested another delivery of spring wine for his table of herbalists. The wine bottles should be on the other side of the festival grounds.\n8\tTalk to Bruidhír at the festival grounds\tBruidhír has called you over to him.\n9\tTalk to Haerandel at the festival grounds\tHaerandel is at the Bree-land Festival Grounds. He has taken an interest in the visiting herbalists, and Bruidhír has asked that you find out what it is, and why.\n",
[591]="70069DF2\n1\tDefeat wolves in the Angle (total: 4)\030Defeat lynx in the Angle (total: 4)\tWolves and lynxes threaten the safety of Ivoreth and Barhador. They can be found on the hill just north of their camp in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n2\tReturn to Ivoreth at her camp\tYou have held off the wolves and lynxes and should return to Ivoreth at her camp in the Angle of Mitheithel to see how she fares.\n",
[592]="70046C31\n1\tTalk to Maendal\tMaendal can be found at Aelin Veren. Chan-két Doloi has offered his knowledge of the Enemy's plans in exchange for the ability to warn his people not to pass through North Ithilien or raise arms against the Rangers. You should speak to Maendal about his plan.\n2\tPlant banners of Far Harad to warn away Haradrim (total: 6)\tIdeal banner locations can be found along the road, in southern North Ithilien. Chan-két Doloi has offered knowledge of the Enemy's movements in exchange for warning his people not to pass through North Ithilien.\n3\tTalk to Chan-két Doloi\tChan-két Doloi can be found at Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien. You have planted the warning banners of Far Harad and should now return to Chan-két Doloi.\n",
[593]="7004E497\n1\tCollect gold-adorned weapons from Jangovar in the Ironfold (total: 12)\tGold-adorned weapons may be carried by any of the Jangovar within the Ironfold. Grámi Hornhelm has asked you to claim the weapons of the Jangovar to provide him and his smiths a swift source of gold.\n2\tDeliver the gold-adorned weapons to Grámi Hornhelm at Hammerstead\tGrámi Hornhelm can be found at Hammerstead. You have collected many gold-adorned weapons from the Jangovar and should now deliver them to Grámi Hornhelm.\n",
[594]="70041361\n1\tInterrogate the resting Corsair\030Interrogate the besotted Corsair\030Interrogate the lazy Corsair\tCorsair drunks can be found in Gaerlond, the ruins of a small fishing village. Collect information from Corsairs in Gaerlond.\n2\tSpeak with Aras near Gaerlond\tAras can be found just outside of Gaerlond. You should speak with Aras.\n",
[595]="70062E7A\n1\tCollect stones from the walls at Sarn Ford (total: 8)\tThe stone walls at Sarn Ford should not miss a few of their number.\n2\tBring the stones to Rothavron at Sarn Ford\tRothavron is at Sarn Ford.\n",
[596]="7004A8F6\n1\tDestroy clusters of spider eggs in Kála-murg (total: 8)\tClusters of spider eggs can be found in shadowed corners of Kála-murg in Rath Cail. You have discovered a number of spider eggs that have gone unnoticed by the Orcs of Kála-murg. You should destroy them before leaving Kála-murg to prevent more Orcs from \"hollowing.\"\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many clusters of spider eggs in Kála-murg.\n",
[597]="70042C75\n1\tFind the Glade of Three Smiling Figures\tThe Glade of Three Smiling Figures is north-east of where you and Bingo camped for the night. Bingo suggested that you might need to return to the road before striking north for the glade.\n2\tTalk to Bingo at the Stone-trolls' Glade\tBingo is in the Stone-trolls' Glade, in the Trollshaws.\n3\tFree the lynx from the trap\tBingo has seen a lynx caught in a cruel trap at the Stone-trolls' Glade, and has asked you to free the poor creature.\n4\tTalk to Bingo at the Stone-trolls' Glade\tBingo is at the Stone-trolls' Glade, in the Trollshaws. You have freed a lynx from a cruel animal trap at Bingo's request, and should speak now to the hobbit.\n5\tTalk to Bingo back on the road south-east of the Stone-trolls' Glade\tBingo wants to return to the road south-east of the Stone-trolls' Glade in order to continue his journey.\n6\tBingo has asked you to wave at the lynx that has followed the two of you back to the road, in order to shoo it away.\t\n7\tTalk to Bingo on the road through the Trollshaws\tBingo is on the road south-east of the Stone-trolls' Glade, in the Trollshaws. You attempted to wave away the lynx that is following Bingo, but the creature refused to leave.\n8\tCollect venison in the Trollshaws (total: 3)\tGlen-hinds and glen-bucks can be found throughout the Trollshaws, and from them you should be able to get the venison that Bingo has requested.\n9\tBring venison to the lynx on the road through the Trollshaws\tWillem Whisker is on the road south-east of the Stone-trolls' Glade. You have collected some venison, and should bring it to the lynx to see if that appeases his hunger.\n10\tTalk to Bingo on the road through the Trollshaws\tBingo is on the road through the Trollshaws, south-east of the Stone-trolls' Glade.\n11\tFind the entrance to Rivendell, the hidden valley\tThe entrance to the hidden valley of Rivendell is marked on Bingo's map, in the eastern heights of the Trollshaws. Bingo is ready to travel to Rivendell, and has suggested that you go to the entrance to that hidden valley.\n12\tTalk to the sentinel at the entrance to the hidden valley\tYou have found the entrance to the hidden valley of Rivendell, and the sentinels eye your small party with suspicion.\n13\tTalk to Bingo at the entrance to the hidden valley\tBingo is outside the entrance to the hidden valley of Rivendell.\n",
[598]="70047D69\n1\tTalk to Faroth\tTalk to Faroth if you would like to take him with you.\n",
[599]="700174FC\n1\tFind a new gear in the tunnels of the Great Wheel\tForeman Indrith believes that you sheared a gear while trying to force the wheel housing in the Great Wheel to start turning once more. He believes another gear is located in the tunnels of the Great Wheel.\n2\tTalk to Indrith\tForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel, south-west of Hulwul-nefekh.\n",
[600]="70054831\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern ithilharn necklace\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern ithilharn necklace.\n2\tTalk to Aldúlf\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn necklace (quantity: see journal) to Aldúlf\030Talk to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn necklace (quantity: see journal) to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[601]="7005482F\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern ithilharn bracelet\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern ithilharn bracelet.\n2\tTalk to Aldúlf\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn bracelet (quantity: see journal) to Aldúlf\030Talk to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn bracelet (quantity: see journal) to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[602]="7005482E\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern ithilharn ring\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Forge a guild-pattern ithilharn ring.\n2\tTalk to Aldúlf\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn ring (quantity: see journal) to Aldúlf\030Talk to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn ring (quantity: see journal) to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[603]="70054830\n1\tExecute the recipe for a guild-pattern ithilharn cabochon\tThe crafting recipes you must create can be bartered for from the Improved Recipes vendor. Create a a guild-pattern ithilharn cabochon.\n2\tTalk to Aldúlf\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn cabochon (quantity: see journal) to Aldúlf\030Talk to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\030Turn in a guild-pattern ithilharn cabochon (quantity: see journal) to the Jeweller's Guild Leader in Minas Morgul\t\n",
[604]="700430D4\n1\tTalk to Glóin at his camp in the Western Bruinen Source area of the Misty Mountains\tGlóin is at his camp in the Western Bruinen Source area of the Misty Mountains. Spalvi has asked you to learn what you can from Glóin about the expedition to Khazad-dûm.\n2\tTalk to Spalvi outside Glóin's camp in the Western Bruinen Source area in the Misty Mountains\tGlóin has told you of the Iron Garrison that seeks to gain entrance to Khazad-dûm, and now you should speak with Spalvi just outside the camp to form a plan.\n3\tTalk to Spalvi at Gwingris, in Eregion\tSpalvi has agreed to travel with you to Gwingris, the ruins in the north-west corner of Eregion, on the next leg of your journey to find Bingo Boffin.\n4\tDefeat bog-lurkers in Eregion (total: 5)\030Defeat Dunlendings in Eregion (total: 5)\tBog-lurkers and Dunlendings can be found throughout Eregion, and they threaten the peace of the area.\n5\tTalk to Spalvi in Gwingris\tYou have made the wilds of Eregion more safe for the Elves at Gwingris, and should return to Spalvi with news of your success.\n6\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in Gwingris\tHaley Meadowsweet has come to the ruins of Gwingris, in north-western Eregion, and wishes to speak with you.\n7\tDefeat half-orcs in or very near to the ruins of Pembar (total: 8)\tThe ruins of Pembar are to the south-east of Gwingris, in Eregion. Haley Meadowsweet sent Theodore Gorse to Pembar to search for treasure (and learn something useful about treasure-seeking), but he has not returned and she fears he may have run afoul of the half-orcs there... or he may have not found Pembar, or he might have gotten lost, or he might have fallen asleep in the brush, or he might have mistaken something for treasure... But if the cause of his delay is indeed half-orc related, she'd like you to handle it.\n8\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in the middle of the ruins of Pembar\tTheodore Gorse is hiding from half-orcs in the middle of the ruins of Pembar, in Eregion.\n9\tBring the half-orc treasure to Haley Meadowsweet in Gwingris\tHaley Meadowsweet is at Gwingris, in north-western Eregion.\n10\tTalk to Spalvi in Gwingris\tSpalvi is at Gwingris, in north-western Eregion, and is waiting to speak to you.\n",
[605]="7004CE27\n1\tTBD\t\n2\tTBD\t\n3\tTalk to Dagrun\t\n",
[606]="70032BDD\n1\tDefeat Globsnaga Orcs (total: 6)\tThe new form of Orc can be found to the east and south-east of Knakk's camp on the elevated walkway.\n2\tReturn to Knakk\tKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[607]="7006CF7F\n1\tComplete the Instance: A New Post\tRaphûz wants to sit with you and discuss over a smoke and food about all that has transpired since his arrival in the Ikorbân Valley.\n2\tSpeak with Raphûz at his post in Wrackwade\tRaphûz was gone in the morning, having headed south to the Wrackwade. Find him there to see how he fares.\n",
[608]="70054881\n1\tAscend the Twisted Stair and present yourself to the Mouth of Sauron\tThe Twisted Stair can be found beyond the halls leading out of the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Zôreth has bidden you to present yourself to the Mouth of Sauron that you might serve in the Dead City.\n2\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Before you were able to reach the Twisted Stair, you encountered Lethi standing amid a slaughter of Men, Orcs, and Stout-axes. You should ask Lethi what has happened.\n",
})
